### 2.2 `/home/lihuzhan/code/2026_0910__op-evolve/op-evolve/knowledge/backends/flydsl/attention/recipes/hd128.md`

**title:** `head_dim=128 flash attention on gfx950, and what a first-class deterministic dQ costs`

**summary:** `"Primus-Turbo's FlyDSL bf16 GQA attention at D=128, measured at main. The default backward accumulates dQ with buffer_atomic_pk_add_bf16 into a permuted bf16 image and is NOT bitwise reproducible; deterministic=True vetoes that onto a split-K band workspace and does deliver bitwise dQ, dK and dV -- verified, five hashed runs. At this head dimension it costs 22.7% of the backward against 11.4% at D=64 measured in the same run, and the factor of two is exactly the kv band the flag also halves. Same operator, head dimension and node as AITER's card 16, opposite branch of the same fork: FlyDSL's deterministic backward is 1.03x AITER's non-deterministic one, and 1.62x its deterministic fallback."`

**applies_to:** `arch: [gfx950]`, `op: [attention]`, `backend: [flydsl]`

**status:** `verified`
**verified:** `"MI355X (gfx950), ROCm 7.2.1, torch 2.10.0+git94c6e04, rocm/primus:v26.3 with flydsl upgraded 0.1.1.dev409 -> 0.2.4, Primus-Turbo ed8d7af4 built from source; 18 op-level rows x 2 determinism settings, 16 kernel-only rows x 3 arms, full profile at B=2 Sq=Skv=4096 Hq=64 Hkv=8 D=128 bf16 bottom-right causal SBHD"`

**`config:` block, verbatim:**

```yaml
config:
  # Mirrors `op.config` in the job spec. A recipe applies only where these match --
  # diff field by field before adopting anything below. Every entry was read out of
  # `can_handle` / `_flydsl_common_ok` / the kernel builders at ed8d7af4, and every
  # head-dimension-dependent one was re-derived here rather than inherited from hd64.md.
  q_head_dim: 128
  kv_head_dim: 128
  heads_q_per_kv: "power of two in [8, 256]"
                                # HARD (`_gqa_group_ok`, attention_impl.py:65-72), and it is a
                                # BACKWARD CORRECTNESS constraint (LD_VEC >= 2), not a tiling
                                # preference. Of the nine head_dim-128 shapes in Turbo's own
                                # model set only three pass it. Outside the range the call goes
                                # to aiter SILENTLY under --backend auto. Measured at G=8 and G=16
  causal: bottom-right          # and it is the ONLY mode. Non-causal is refused, not slowed
  sliding_window: "left only, W >= 64, or none"
                                # `(W,0)` or `(-1,-1)`. A window also makes `deterministic` a
                                # NO-OP -- `_dq_a16_for` requires window_left < 0. Measured
                                # +0.01% at W=1024 and -0.03% at W=512
  sparsity: dense               # the sparse-MLA path is a different pair of kernels
  format: "[thd-varlen (uniform cu_seqlens only), sbhd]"
                                # dense is SBHD-ONLY; bshd is accepted at batch 1 alone, where
                                # the bytes coincide (`_sbhd_layout`), and refused above it
  direction: [fwd, bwd]
  dtype:
    qkv: bf16                   # hard; fp16 is refused
    acc: fp32
    dq_accum: "bf16 atomic (default) | fp32 split-K reduce (deterministic=True)"
  softmax_scale: "1/sqrt(D), baked"   # any other value is refused (`_scale_ok`)
  sink: "optional, fp32 [Hq]"   # ⚠ NOT EXERCISED HERE. On THIS card's backend (flydsl) the
                                # pair sink + `deterministic` is LEGAL. A previous revision
                                # said flatly "mutually exclusive with `deterministic` by
                                # assertion"; the assertion is real but it guards the AITER
                                # path, and flydsl returns before reaching it. Section 12b
  determinism: "dQ NOT reproducible by default; `deterministic=True` DOES deliver bitwise dQ/dK/dV and costs 22.7%"
                                # THE FIELD THIS CARD EXISTS FOR. dK, dV and the forward are
                                # bitwise in BOTH settings on every shape measured. dQ is not,
                                # by default, on every full-causal square SBHD shape: five
                                # identical runs give five distinct dQ. Section 3
  seqlen: ">= 512 measured; no gate"
                                # `seq_len >= 384` is a stale docstring, not a gate (card 8).
                                # But `Skv % 256 == 0` IS a gate on the atomic path, so a
                                # non-aligned Skv is reproducible by accident
  power_regime: "forward power-capped, backward clock-capped"
                                # 1853 MHz at 1324 W forward; 2142 MHz at 1298 W backward.
                                # The deterministic backward draws MORE (1377 W of 1400) at the
                                # same clock -- the extra is DRAM traffic. Section 4
  grid_fill: "B x ceil(Skv/BLOCK_KV) x Hkv x q_split work-groups"
                                # 1024 default / 512 per chunk deterministic, at b2/s4096/Hkv8
  tuned_for: sweep              # constants are a compromise across a shape set
```

