## 4. `knowledge/ops/attention/` — full listing

Five files. All `status: reference`, `applies_to: arch [any] / backend [any]`, no measurements anywhere by design.

| File | Lines | Summary |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `README.md` | 74 | Branch contract. Table routing each of the four content files to the moment you read it. States the boundary test: "**if the statement would change on a different GPU, or in a different DSL, it does not belong here.**" Structural ratios (FLOP counts, reuse factors, causal-block fractions) belong; measurements do not. Explicitly points tile/wave/occupancy questions at `backends/flydsl/attention/recipes/hd64.md`, dead ends at `backends/flydsl/attention/dead-ends.md`, issue-port model at `backends/flydsl/attention/techniques.md`. **"What is not covered":** sparse/block-sparse selection, latent/compressed KV (MLA), decode-time single-query shapes, cross-attention — "treating this directory's mask and parallelism arithmetic as applying to them would be wrong." Your job is dense/causal/GQA, so it is in scope. |
| `online-softmax.md` | 223 | The definitional form vs the one-pass recurrence; the rescale and its cost; shift invariance and what it licenses; LSE and what storing it saves; degenerate/fully-masked rows; where precision must be held wider than storage; non-associativity and the price of reproducibility. Sections: "The definitional form, and why it is not the one you implement", "The one-pass recurrence", "Shift invariance, and what it licenses", "LSE, and what storing it saves", "Degenerate rows and fully-masked blocks", "Where precision must be held", "Non-associativity, and what it costs to be reproducible". |
| `backward-dataflow.md` | 205 | **The most relevant file for your `direction: bwd`.** Five matrix products plus one row-wise reduction; the identity that makes the backward one-pass; why the row term (`sum(O*dO)` / delta) is formed before the main loop; **why one of dQ or dK/dV always needs atomics or a split-and-reduce**; what the loop order (KV-outer vs Q-outer) also decides; arithmetic intensity of the backward; why the backward is hard to make deterministic. |
| `masking-heads-and-layout.md` | 311 | **The second most relevant.** Causal masking and its block classification / work imbalance; a dedicated `### Top-left versus bottom-right alignment` section (lines 75-105) — directly load-bearing for your `causal=bottom-right` vs the HipKittens cards' top-left; sliding windows; `## Head grouping: MHA, GQA, MQA` and what GQA does to a KV-outer kernel's parallelism; `## Head dimension, and where the arithmetic intensity is` (why d=64 is harder than d=128); `## Sequence layout` covering bshd/sbhd/bhsd/varlen. README says read it "at setup, when the job spec's `op.config` is first read, and again whenever a constant is carried across a configuration." |
| `reference-implementation.md` | 150 | What an obviously-correct eager reference must get right; where a library reference legitimately disagrees (convention, not bug); whether a library kernel can be a bitwise oracle (it cannot, in general); what the acceptance set must contain; how to get reference gradients for the backward. |

**There is no `techniques.md` or `dead-ends.md` under `ops/attention/`** — by design; those genres live under `backends/<backend>/attention/`. The only ones that exist for attention anywhere are `backends/flydsl/attention/techniques.md` and `backends/flydsl/attention/dead-ends.md` (both `measured elsewhere (Primus-Turbo PR #458, MI355X)`, scope `gfx950, attention, flydsl`):

- `techniques.md` (439 lines): "The constraint is softmax issue, not matrix throughput"; "The pipes are partly additive — measure the conversion rate"; "Two ways to overlap exp with MFMA"; "Which cluster the work lands in"; "How you spell the transcendental changes the schedule"; "One `vmcnt`, shared by loads and stores" (← explicitly invalidated on gfx1250, see §6); "Working out your occupancy limiter"; "Audit the index map before the kernel body"; "Filling the grid" / "How many bytes a split costs is set by the register file"; "Determinism without float atomics"; "MFMA shape as a scheduling knob" (← no MFMA on gfx1250).
- `dead-ends.md` (427 lines), 19 recorded losses: software exp polynomial; fp8 operands; manual wave staggering; splitting the head dimension in a KV-outer backward; enlarging the KV block (cost 3x); forcing occupancy by raising the request; LDS double-buffering of streamed K/V; non-temporal hints on reused operands; deleting never-issued instructions; a non-amortising register transpose; hand-written address arithmetic; an autotune bound inherited from an earlier configuration; an opaque inline-asm transcendental carrying no hazard; coarsening a hazard anchor ("faster, wrong, and invisible on the main shape"); a sync-count change validated on one shape; a probe that deletes the exp; a win measured on one shape class; a tile heuristic keyed to the wrong axis; a gate whose comment cannot state a reason; and "A dead end without a root cause".

`backends/aiter/attention/README.md` exists (structural note on the 286-object / 11-manifest `fmha_v3_bwd` family, and "Not filled yet: a `techniques.md` and a `dead-ends.md`"). **`backends/hipkittens/attention/` has no README.md** — only the two recipes.

